@startuml single-signal-path
title US-06: Single Signal Path - Only One Weak Signal Present, No Composite Raised

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Signal loss only - no proximity event ==

Evaluator -> Redis : check entity:live:VesselB
Redis --> Evaluator : key missing - VesselB is dark

Evaluator -> Neo4j : MATCH (b:Entity {id: "VesselB"})-[e:PROXIMITY_EVENT]->(a)\nWHERE e.timestamp_ms > $dark_since_ms\nAND NOT (b)-[:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(a)\nRETURN a, e
Neo4j --> Evaluator : no results

note over Evaluator
  VesselB is dark but has not appeared
  near any unrelated entity.
  Only one weak signal present.
  No composite alert raised.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish individual SIGNAL_LOSS alert\n{ type: SIGNAL_LOSS, entity_id: VesselB }

== Proximity only - no prior signal loss ==

Evaluator -> Redis : check entity:live:VesselC
Redis --> Evaluator : VesselC is live (key present)

note over Evaluator
  VesselC is in proximity to VesselD
  but has not gone dark.
  No signal loss component.
  Only one weak signal present.
  No composite alert raised.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish individual UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY alert\n{ type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  entity_c, entity_d }

note over Kafka
  Composite alert requires BOTH:
  signal loss AND proximity to an
  unrelated entity within the loss window.
  Neither case above qualifies.
end note

@enduml
